{
  "$comment": [
    "Cross-language parity corpus. Loaded by BOTH test suites — src/__tests__/parity.test.ts",
    "and crates/clickhouse-kit/tests/parity.rs — so the TypeScript and Rust ports of the same",
    "behaviour are checked against one committed set of expectations rather than two",
    "hand-mirrored ones.",
    "",
    "Why it exists: the two flatteners disagreed for months and both suites were green, because",
    "each asserted its own behaviour. TS reached {'a.b': '{\"c\":1}'} at maxDepth 1; Rust needed",
    "max_depth 2 for the identical input and output. Nothing compared them, so nothing said so.",
    "",
    "Scope: the pure, deterministic surface both languages implement — flatten, the column-type",
    "allowlist, and identifier validation. The migration runner and drift gate also exist in both,",
    "but they are I/O against a live ClickHouse; their agreement is covered by the Rust",
    "testcontainers suites rather than here.",
    "",
    "Adding a case here is the point: it must pass in every language or the build is red."
  ],

  "flatten": {
    "$comment": [
      "flattenRecord (TS) / flatten_record (Rust). `options` are always given in full so no case",
      "depends on a default that could diverge. Key order is not compared — the result is a map —",
      "but WHICH keys survive a maxKeys truncation is, so both implementations iterate a node's",
      "keys in sorted order.",
      "",
      "maxDepth counts levels of RECURSION, not frames: the root object is always destructured,",
      "and maxDepth 0 means every one of its values is a leaf."
    ],
    "cases": [
      {
        "name": "nested objects become dotted keys",
        "input": { "a": 1, "b": { "c": 2, "d": { "e": "x" } } },
        "options": { "maxDepth": 8, "maxKeys": 1024, "delimiter": "." },
        "expected": { "a": "1", "b.c": "2", "b.d.e": "x" }
      },
      {
        "name": "arrays are JSON-stringified, never recursed",
        "input": { "tags": ["a", "b"], "nested": { "ids": [1, 2] } },
        "options": { "maxDepth": 8, "maxKeys": 1024, "delimiter": "." },
        "expected": { "tags": "[\"a\",\"b\"]", "nested.ids": "[1,2]" }
      },
      {
        "name": "strings pass through unquoted; other primitives stringify",
        "input": { "s": "hello", "n": 42, "b": true, "z": null },
        "options": { "maxDepth": 8, "maxKeys": 1024, "delimiter": "." },
        "expected": { "s": "hello", "n": "42", "b": "true", "z": "null" }
      },
      {
        "name": "a string containing the delimiter is not re-split",
        "input": { "path": "a.b.c" },
        "options": { "maxDepth": 8, "maxKeys": 1024, "delimiter": "." },
        "expected": { "path": "a.b.c" }
      },
      {
        "name": "custom delimiter",
        "input": { "a": { "b": 1 } },
        "options": { "maxDepth": 8, "maxKeys": 1024, "delimiter": "__" },
        "expected": { "a__b": "1" }
      },
      {
        "name": "depth cap 1 — recurse once, then stringify the remaining subtree",
        "input": { "a": { "b": { "c": 1 } } },
        "options": { "maxDepth": 1, "maxKeys": 1024, "delimiter": "." },
        "expected": { "a.b": "{\"c\":1}" }
      },
      {
        "name": "depth cap 2 — recurse twice",
        "input": { "a": { "b": { "c": { "d": 1 } } } },
        "options": { "maxDepth": 2, "maxKeys": 1024, "delimiter": "." },
        "expected": { "a.b.c": "{\"d\":1}" }
      },
      {
        "name": "depth cap 0 — the root is still destructured, its values are all leaves",
        "input": { "a": { "b": 1 }, "c": 2 },
        "options": { "maxDepth": 0, "maxKeys": 1024, "delimiter": "." },
        "expected": { "a": "{\"b\":1}", "c": "2" }
      },
      {
        "name": "an empty object at the depth cap stringifies to {}",
        "input": { "a": {} },
        "options": { "maxDepth": 0, "maxKeys": 1024, "delimiter": "." },
        "expected": { "a": "{}" }
      },
      {
        "name": "key cap truncates deterministically — sorted order, never exceeded",
        "input": { "d": 4, "b": 2, "a": 1, "c": 3 },
        "options": { "maxDepth": 8, "maxKeys": 2, "delimiter": "." },
        "expected": { "a": "1", "b": "2" }
      },
      {
        "name": "key cap counts leaves, not source keys",
        "input": { "a": { "x": 1, "y": 2 }, "b": 3 },
        "options": { "maxDepth": 8, "maxKeys": 2, "delimiter": "." },
        "expected": { "a.x": "1", "a.y": "2" }
      }
    ]
  },

  "columnTypes": {
    "$comment": [
      "columnFromTypeSpec (TS) / ColumnTypeSpec::to_ch_type (Rust). `chType` is the exact",
      "ClickHouse type string both must render. `rejected: true` means untrusted input naming it",
      "must NOT produce a column — TS throws SchemaSafetyError, Rust fails to deserialize,",
      "because the disallowed types have no representation in the enum. Different mechanism,",
      "same guarantee, and that is what the corpus pins."
    ],
    "cases": [
      { "name": "String", "spec": "String", "chType": "String" },
      { "name": "UUID", "spec": "UUID", "chType": "UUID" },
      { "name": "Bool", "spec": "Bool", "chType": "Bool" },
      { "name": "Date", "spec": "Date", "chType": "Date" },
      { "name": "DateTime", "spec": "DateTime", "chType": "DateTime" },
      {
        "name": "bare DateTime64 defaults to millisecond precision",
        "spec": "DateTime64",
        "chType": "DateTime64(3)"
      },
      { "name": "Int8", "spec": "Int8", "chType": "Int8" },
      { "name": "Int64", "spec": "Int64", "chType": "Int64" },
      { "name": "UInt64", "spec": "UInt64", "chType": "UInt64" },
      { "name": "Float64", "spec": "Float64", "chType": "Float64" },
      { "name": "JSON", "spec": "JSON", "chType": "JSON" },
      {
        "name": "Nullable wrapper",
        "spec": { "nullable": "String" },
        "chType": "Nullable(String)"
      },
      {
        "name": "LowCardinality wrapper",
        "spec": { "lowCardinality": "String" },
        "chType": "LowCardinality(String)"
      },
      {
        "name": "wrappers compose, outermost first",
        "spec": { "lowCardinality": { "nullable": "String" } },
        "chType": "LowCardinality(Nullable(String))"
      },
      {
        "name": "Nullable around the DateTime64 default",
        "spec": { "nullable": "DateTime64" },
        "chType": "Nullable(DateTime64(3))"
      },
      { "name": "Array(String)", "spec": { "array": "String" }, "chType": "Array(String)" },
      {
        "name": "Map(String, String) — note the space",
        "spec": { "map": ["String", "String"] },
        "chType": "Map(String, String)"
      },

      { "name": "Decimal is not allowlisted", "spec": "Decimal", "rejected": true },
      { "name": "FixedString is not allowlisted", "spec": "FixedString(16)", "rejected": true },
      { "name": "Enum is not allowlisted", "spec": "Enum8('a' = 1)", "rejected": true },
      {
        "name": "a raw type expression is not allowlisted",
        "spec": "String) --",
        "rejected": true
      },
      { "name": "lowercase is not the allowlisted spelling", "spec": "string", "rejected": true },
      { "name": "Array of a non-String element", "spec": { "array": "Int32" }, "rejected": true },
      {
        "name": "Map with a non-String key",
        "spec": { "map": ["Int32", "String"] },
        "rejected": true
      },
      {
        "name": "Map with a non-String value",
        "spec": { "map": ["String", "Int32"] },
        "rejected": true
      },
      { "name": "an unrecognised wrapper", "spec": { "tuple": "String" }, "rejected": true },
      {
        "name": "a disallowed type inside a wrapper",
        "spec": { "nullable": "Decimal" },
        "rejected": true
      }
    ]
  },

  "identifiers": {
    "$comment": [
      "validateIdentifier (TS) / validate_identifier (Rust). One strict ASCII allowlist:",
      "^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*$ within the length bound. This is the gate that makes an",
      "untrusted column name unable to inject SQL, so both languages must reject identically —",
      "a name one side accepts and the other rejects is a portability bug at a security boundary.",
      "`maxIdentifierLength` is the default (128)."
    ],
    "cases": [
      { "value": "org_id", "valid": true },
      { "value": "_leading_underscore", "valid": true },
      { "value": "Mixed_Case_9", "valid": true },
      { "value": "a", "valid": true },

      { "value": "", "valid": false, "why": "empty" },
      { "value": "9leading_digit", "valid": false, "why": "must not start with a digit" },
      { "value": "has space", "valid": false, "why": "space" },
      { "value": "has-hyphen", "valid": false, "why": "hyphen" },
      { "value": "has.dot", "valid": false, "why": "dot — would address another table" },
      { "value": "has`backtick", "valid": false, "why": "backtick — quoting escape" },
      { "value": "has\"quote", "valid": false, "why": "double quote" },
      { "value": "has'quote", "valid": false, "why": "single quote" },
      { "value": "drop; DROP TABLE t", "valid": false, "why": "statement separator" },
      { "value": "a--comment", "valid": false, "why": "SQL comment" },
      { "value": "café", "valid": false, "why": "non-ASCII" },
      { "value": "emoji_🙂", "valid": false, "why": "non-ASCII" },
      { "value": "tab\there", "valid": false, "why": "control character" },
      { "value": "nul\u0000byte", "valid": false, "why": "NUL" },
      {
        "value": "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa",
        "valid": false,
        "why": "129 characters — one over the 128 bound"
      }
    ]
  }
}
